Epilogue 3
Me: Are you ready to send them back to the past?
Scarlet: You know, now that this conflict is resolved, why don't you come back to the past with me? You saved me and I want to see what my life back then would have looked like. With you.
(t): That's a really big question.
Me: What about the company? And about the gang?
Scarlet: We can build something new together. The company will be fine, I can leave it to Seth. And Ray was supposed to take over the gang at some point anyway. And I know Lu will keep them mentally sane.
I look at the trio.
Lu: I will miss you, boss. But I think we all want you to be happy.
Seth just nods.
Ray: He's right! As long as ya'll are happy nothin' matters.
He gives us a big grin.
(t): I guess things will be fine here. and we might be back in the future anyways!
I turn to Scarlet.
Me: That sounds wonderful, Scarlet. There's just one thing.
For a second Scarlet looks scared.
Scarlet: What is it?
Me: I won't live as long as you do. I'm just a human after all…
TIME SKIP, NEW SCENE
Two years later, in the past.
Me: You know, it's kind of a shame.
Scarlet: What is? I think this is perfect.
ILLUSTRATION
We gaze up at the big red moon in the sky while swirling the red liquid in our glasses.
Me: It's just… I miss the feeling of getting my blood sucked. It only happened twice in my life.
Scarlet: Oh, you! One time was a situation that couldn't be helped and the other time was when I turned you. That's more than enough.
Me: Have you ever had your blood sucked by anyone?
Scarlet: No, I was born a vampire after all.
Me: Then you wouldn't know!
Scarlet laughs at me.
Me: Want me to try it out on you?
Scarlet: Vampire blood won't feed you.
Me: That might be so. But maybe it'll make us feel good?
We glance at each other and laugh together this time.
Scarlet: Okay, fine. But later. Right now, let's enjoy this view a bit longer.
Me: You're right. Today's blood moon is beautiful. But its beauty pales in comparison to yours.
Scarlet: Stop it!
(t): She's embarrassed. How cute.
It's a shame I can't see her blush in this dim, red light.
